    },
    "q-111909": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111909",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/c64cfa701997c2b9e5e54f7eb77afb9927b878065af9c32fed86f09f140a4ec4.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{5}).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{5})$ on our diagram. Let's also consider the region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/056fcbe25f83f488e1a88988d577535d0ef3776442f83e7d81560c6145f466a3.png)\n\nUsing the definition of the joint CDF, we have\n\n$$\nF(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{5})=P(X<\\frac{1}{2},Y<\\frac{1}{5})={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/5}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/2}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{5}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/5}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/2}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(u+v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/5}{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+uv]}_{u=0}^{u=1/2}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/5}(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{v}{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[\\frac{v}{8}+\\frac{{v}^{2}}{4}]}_{v=0}^{v=1/5} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{40}+\\frac{1}{100}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{200}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111909-a",
