    "q-111911": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111911",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x,y),$ where\n\n$$\nF(10,9)=0.7,\\,F(10,5)=0.2,\\,F(8,9)=0.3,\\,F(8,5)=0.1.\n$$\n\nFind $P(8\\le X\\le 10,5\\le Y\\le 9).$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $F(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)$ is the probability that the pair $(X,Y)$ will lie inside the infinite rectangular region that has its top-right corner at $(x,y)$ and whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axes.\n\nLet's sketch the region corresponding to the probability we wish to find.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/6d99e5e84349bb1279f4a105a6611b55a85e41aa2bf96e1dc28a8a343e0d9432.png)\n\nGeometrically, this region can be obtained as follows:\n\n1\\. Take the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(10,9).$\n\n2\\. Subtract the infinite rectangles that have their top-right corners at $(10,5)$ and $(8,9).$\n\n3\\. Finally, we need to *add back* the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(8,5).$ This is because we subtracted this region twice in step 2.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8\\le X\\le 10,5\\le Y\\le 9) & =\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(10,9)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 10,Y\\le 9)}} \\\\  & \\,-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(10,5)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 10,Y\\le 5)}}-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(8,9)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 8,Y\\le 9)}} \\\\  & \\,+\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(8,5)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 8,Y\\le 5)}} \\\\  & =F(10,9)-F(10,5)-F(8,9)+F(8,5) \\\\  & =0.7-0.2-0.3+0.1 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111911-a",
