    "q-143658": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143658",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{e}^{y}, & -1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>2,\\,y>\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $x>2,\\,y>\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/19510c5eb927edbc93ff077f13e645820548e9074da0e1101d9ef641650642bb.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=D.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo our region $Δ$ covers the entire region where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={∬}_{D}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
