    "q-143697": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143697",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}x{e}^{y}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡4, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡4,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/c62b7e0866443343399eb9de04a58bdec5095c21492cb5b65062de4faafc2a10.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le x,\\,0\\le v\\le y\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{6}u{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{v}{\\int }_{0}^{x}u\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{v}{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=x}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}[{e}^{v}]_{v=0}^{v=y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}({e}^{y}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
