    "q-143713": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143713",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}xy, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $y>2.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $y>2$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/bd8ba5862859dd85230edaeeeaef011fc163caf58d24ee0a9f64e6cda2a8ac63.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le x,\\,1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{3}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}v{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=x}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{v{x}^{2}}{2}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{v=1}^{v=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}({2}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
