    "q-143716": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143716",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2}+y, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $y>1.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $y>1$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/12e26559137d7c494c5ddc6f1add55f646dd84236f355221042448ddeacd2879.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le x,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{x}u{v}^{2}+v\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}{2}+uv]}_{u=1}^{u=x}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{{x}^{2}{v}^{2}}{2}+xv-\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}-v]\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{{v}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)}{2}+v(x-1)]\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{v}^{3}({x}^{2}-1)}{6}+\\frac{{v}^{2}(x-1)}{2}]}_{v=0}^{v=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{6}+\\frac{x-1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
