    "q-143712": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143712",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}, & 1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>3$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $x>3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274884/assets/1fbbe9e4728cd5aefcc456a6c8666e3e2e6c0d0bc832f471677d908cf6c012e3.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 3,\\,1\\le v\\le y\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{1}^{y}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{y}v{[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{u=1}^{u=3}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{y}v(1-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{y}\\frac{2}{3}v\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{v=1}^{v=y} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({y}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
